<BaseLayout title="Squadfire — Terms of Use" description="Terms of Use of Squadfire, a game by Little Monge Studios">
  <h1>Squadfire — Terms of Use</h1>
  <p class="muted">Last updated: 2026-10-03</p>

  <h2>1. About these terms</h2>
  <p>Squadfire is developed by an individual developer operating as "Little Monge Studios" (Spain). By using the app you agree to these terms. If you do not agree, please do not use Squadfire. Contact: <a href="mailto:team@littlemongestudios.com">team@littlemongestudios.com</a>.</p>

  <h2>2. Who can use Squadfire</h2>
  <p>You must be at least 13 years old (or the minimum age required in your country). You are responsible for your account and for what is done with it.</p>

  <h2>3. Usernames</h2>
  <p>Your username is visible to other players on the leaderboards and in your public profile. It must not: be offensive, hateful, sexual or violent; harass or impersonate anyone; include personal data (yours or someone else’s, such as full names, phone numbers or addresses); or advertise anything. Offensive usernames are rejected automatically, and we may reset any username that breaks these rules — you will then be asked to choose a new one.</p>

  <h2>4. Conduct</h2>
  <p>Do not use Squadfire to harass, threaten or spam other players (including through pokes, squad invitations or invite codes), do not try to cheat the streak, points, squad or ranking systems (for example by repeatedly changing your device’s time zone), do not exploit bugs, and do not try to access other people’s accounts or data.</p>

  <h2>5. Reporting and blocking</h2>
  <p>You can report a player from their public profile if you think they break these terms, and block them so they disappear from your lists and can no longer poke you. Blocking also removes the friendship, and you can no longer be in the same squad. Reports are reviewed manually; abusing the report feature is itself a breach of these terms.</p>

  <h2>6. Consequences</h2>
  <p>Depending on the seriousness, we may reset your username, remove content, or suspend or delete accounts that break these terms, without compensation for points or cosmetic items.</p>

  <h2>7. Points, cosmetics and purchases</h2>
  <p>Points and cosmetic items are part of the game: they have no monetary value, cannot be exchanged for money and cannot be transferred. Nothing you buy gives an advantage in the rankings. A streak wager only puts points at stake, its result depends solely on your own check-ins and it involves no chance and no real money. Real-money purchases (streak freeze packs) are processed by Google Play under its own terms.</p>

  <h2>8. Your data</h2>
  <p>How we handle your data is explained in the <a href="/squadfire/privacy/">Privacy Policy</a>. You can delete your account at any time from Settings.</p>

  <h2>9. Changes</h2>
  <p>We may update these terms. If the changes are significant, the app will ask you to accept the new version before you keep using it.</p>
</BaseLayout>
